This program is supposed to end with a status: `exit_now(7)` under
`with_exit_real` asks for 7, and 7 is what both backends have to hand the
shell. Without this marker run.sh reads the non-zero JVM exit as a failed run
and blocks `diff`, `stderr` and `exit` -- which is the whole of what this file
checks, since the two backends' stdout already agreed while the bug was live.
The code is still compared between them; the marker says "non-zero is expected
here", never "any exit will do". See the header of run.sh.
